From db1cc976571af490a0854dc51738b179527b8643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Ant body: the appetite gate becomes a gene (slot 28), and
 a birth's body mutation is one shared function

What it does: an ant's crop can now inherit how hard it holds back digesting
while the ant is fed -- the appetite gate the teacher lane found brings far
more food home in the training bed, but which no lineage could reach because
digestion is a body rule and the brain cannot touch it. Owner, 2026-10-22:
"The body should be able to mutate too."

- organism::TRAIT_APPETITE (slot 27, CREATURE_TRAITS 27 -> 28): the gate's
  weight is digest_hunger_weight + allele, clamped 0..1 (creature::
  appetite_weight_of). Additive, no species gate, per the sight-range ruling.
  Width 0 on every species, so nothing drifts in the game.
- creature::mutate_traits: the body half of mutate_newborn, split out
  unchanged (same draws in the same order, width-0 slots take none), so a
  harness that places its own children mutates a body by the game's rule.
- creature::inherit_body: a parent's body onto a placed child, mutated on
  the child's own birth stream (RNG_SLOT_BIRTH), for the in-run bed.
- Every species file authors the new slot at 0.0; lab names it
  (APPETITE GATE / appetite row).

Measured: bit-identical. In-run bed, hA1 founders, 200k frames, seeds 1 and
2, against the compute branch at 98ad9dc4: events, births, sel and stock
files byte-identical with the gate off; with hungergate=1 digest_bar=3
(the species gate on, read through the new function) also byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DWLmVnMuZT7iPWY73DvPhf
